	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The following description is about the account payable process. It begins when you file a copy for internal records. 
Once filing a copy for internal records occurs, creating a receiving report should be done. 
Once creating a receiving report occurs, one or more of the following paths should be executed: doubling check a three-way match, confirming all documents have been amended, gathering the receiving report. 
After confirming all documents have been amended, one or more of the following paths should be executed: reporting errors to relevant team member, gathering the vendors invoice. 
Afterwards, the next tasks should be checking dates to avoid penalty charges and scheduling the payment, they should be done in parallel. 
When checking dates to avoid penalty charges is completed, one or more of the following paths should be executed: storing in paid invoice file, entering the invoice into the accounts payable account. 
The process is now completed. 
"
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The following description is about the account payable process, which starts when you file a copy for internal documents.
Once a copy of a document appears for internal records, it should be done creating a receiving report.
Once a receiving report is created, one or more of the following paths should be executed: doubling a three-way match, confirming all documents are amended and gathering the receiving report.
After confirmation that all documents have been amended, one or more of the following paths should be executed: reporting the errors to the relevant team member, gathering the vendor invoice.
The next tasks should then be checking dates to avoid penalty charges and scheduling the payment - they should be done in parallel.
When the checking of dates is completed to avoid penalty charges, one or more of the following paths should be executed: depositing in the invoice file, entering the invoice into the accounts payable account.
The process is now complete.
"
